# Still — @still/ext-chromium build-time env (Vite `import.meta.env`, baked in by `wxt build`).
#
# Copy to `packages/ext-chromium/.env` and fill in. NEVER commit a real value — only this template
# is tracked (.gitignore ignores `.env.*` and excepts `.env.example`). Legend as in the root
# .env.example ([loop-ok] etc.).
#
# Fail-safe build-mode gate (docs/solutions/security-issues/gate-production-trust-by-build-mode.md):
# leave these BLANK and the built extension simply ships WITHOUT the auth/purchase spine and
# without the OTA rule-set fetch. Atomic local blocking and the bundled rule seed remain usable
# without an account; there is no sign-in capability and deliberately NO dev fallback.

# [loop-ok] Public Supabase project URL + anon key (safe in client bundles; RLS is the real
# boundary). Powers the background-owned Supabase session (email-OTP sign-in, create-web-checkout,
# reconcile-entitlement, settings sync) and the signed rule-set refresh.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# Configured cloud builds keep legacy optional free settings sync by default. Only the exact
# packaged value "true" opts into modern canonical sync and its paired committed popup, after
# the target backend supports the canonical receipt protocol. Blank/false/invalid stays legacy.
# No production activation is implied by source support. Without valid Supabase config, atomic
# local blocking remains available and no cloud client is created.
VITE_MODERN_SETTINGS_SYNC_ENABLED=

# [loop-ok] Optional scoped-access verification inputs; public environment and JSON key allowlist
# only ({kid, publicKeyHex, purpose, environment}). Never place issuer signing material here.
# Blank keeps default production trust with no access keys; no paid-sale activation is implied.
VITE_ACCESS_ENVIRONMENT=
VITE_ACCESS_PUBLIC_KEYS=

# Product analytics (ADR 0004). The project key is public by design (it can only send events).
# Blank → no analytics and no "Share usage data" switch.
VITE_POSTHOG_KEY=
VITE_POSTHOG_HOST=https://us.i.posthog.com
